      "title": "Cargo Cult Science",
      "gist": "Science needs a habit of leaning over backwards to show how you might be wrong, and fields lacking it only imitate science.",
      "question": "Cargo Cult Science — why do fields that look scientific fail without a strict honesty about being wrong? (a talk with examples)"
